"""
MULTI-TYPE ANALYZER v3 - your full analysis + honest validation layer
====================================================================
What changed from your previous version (everything else is unchanged):

P0  Walk-forward backtest. Each method predicts draw t using ONLY draws
    before t, then is scored against draw t. (The old backtest_hits()
    scored a prediction against the same draws it was built from.)
P0  Exact random baseline per game type, and Benjamini-Hochberg (BH)
    correction across EVERY type x method tested in the run.
P0  Number range comes from TYPE_CONFIG, not from whatever draws are
    loaded (old: Type4 could never pick 42, Type6 never 49, Type7 never 51-55).
P1  find_best() picks only a method that clears BH < 0.05 with enough
    trials. Otherwise it prints "NO EDGE" - all picks have equal odds.
P1  Every pick is finalized: pool types = 6 unique numbers in range,
    positional types = n digits in range, order kept, never sorted.

Bug fixes:
  - CustomLinearRegression ALWAYS had slope 0 (numpy shape broadcast), so
    every "ML Regression" in the old script returned the plain average.
    This is why the difference model always predicted +1 on every ball.
  - String sorting of "SET_n" keys (SET_9 sorted after SET_10) in
    FunctionalClassifier and LagMemoryEngine -> numeric sort.
  - Even/Odd regression could predict a negative count -> crash. Clamped.
  - Segment combo filled with random numbers then de-duplicated, so it
    could return < 6 numbers. Now finalized.
  - Ensemble no longer counts Best Scored; Weighted Consensus no longer
    counts the Ensemble vote (no method votes for its own output).
  - LagMemoryEngine ranges/element count now follow the game type.
  - RNGCracker removed: it was never called, its LCG/LFSR checks always
    returned None, and its "MT" path just returned seeded random numbers.
  - Half-size candidate subsets removed: they were always filtered out.
  - UPS banner no longer hard-coded to "SET_24".
  - Deep learning is OFF by default and labeled UNVALIDATED (too slow to
    walk-forward). Turn on with RUN_DEEP_LEARNING = True.

HOW TO USE (Colab or terminal)
  1. Put history in data_types (oldest first) or point CSV_PATHS at files
     (one draw per line). The draw you want to predict must NOT be in it.
  2. Optional: after the draw, put the result in RESULTS to score picks.
     RESULTS is never merged into history.
  3. Run. Optional terminal flags: --selftest, --quick (skip backtest).

A method marked "no edge" has no demonstrated advantage over a random
ticket. A method that clears BH describes past data, not the next draw.
"""
